Thanks to all those that answered my previous post.

To recap, I have two 9 track tapes that have hand written labels
BRUSYS backup_set: MPLUSKIT and BRUSYS backup_set M+KIT2. When I mount
them on a VAX the label on the tape seems to be BACKUP; I can make a
disk image with VMSTPCE. I can also read both tapes and images with
BRUREAD.
 
I tried to create a TK50 boot tape with VMSTPC and several combinations
of
qualifiers, but when I try to boot the TK50 on a 11/73 I always get
a Message 11 No bootable media in drive.

One possible problem could be that RSX11M+ does not support booting
from a TK50, but I don't thing this is the problem. My impression is
that
the tape must contain some special stuff somewhere so that the boot
firmware recognizes it as bootable.

What special requirements does a bootable TK50 have? 512 blocks ? ...

Help!

TIA

