As far as I remember a RSX11m(+) distribution consists a bootable RSX11S
medium (or saveset?) with all needed utilities to initialize and test (bad) a
blank disk, and a second medium (or saveset) with a minimum RSX11M(+) system
able to do a sysgen.
Because the bootable system is a RSX11S you have to know the RSX11S
MCR-syntax (-> tas /  run ini / run brusys / ... ).
I remember a TK50 where both savesets were on the same tape.

Werner

